{"id":"180e55a5516174c6","group":"58","path":"58/batch04/58-df-large-embedding.md","title":"Large Embedding","display":"df-large-embedding — Large Embedding","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-large-embedding","aliases":["58-df-large-embedding"],"display":"df-large-embedding — Large Embedding","depends_on":["[[../batch03/58-df-large-cardinal.md]]","[[../batch11/58-df-class.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md]]","[[58-df-class-embedding-data.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-large-embedding"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-large-embedding</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-large-embedding — Large Embedding"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"6a8560d21b03f127\" href=\"?note=6a8560d21b03f127\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-large-cardinal.md\">../batch03/58-df-large-cardinal.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ca2a9c9166fa8cce\" href=\"?note=ca2a9c9166fa8cce\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-class.md\">../batch11/58-df-class.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md\">../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"5578254565969219\" href=\"?note=5578254565969219\" title=\"58-df-class-embedding-data.md\">58-df-class-embedding-data.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,j\">\\(M,j\\)</span> (definable-class parameters)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Class}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Class}_S\\)</span> (definable-class predicate from dependency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ordinal}\">\\(\\mathrm{Ordinal}\\)</span> is the ordinal predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md\">../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md</a></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ClassFunction}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\">\\(\\mathrm{ClassFunction}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ElementaryClassEmbedding}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\">\\(\\mathrm{ElementaryClassEmbedding}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\)</span> 与 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{crit}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\">\\(\\operatorname{crit}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\)</span> 采用 <code>58-df-class-embedding-data</code>。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ElementaryEmbedding}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j,(V,\\in),(M,\\in))\">\\(\\mathrm{ElementaryEmbedding}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j,(V,\\in),(M,\\in))\\)</span> 是下式定义的结构记法。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{crit}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j)\">\\(\\operatorname{crit}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j)\\)</span> is the least ordinal moved by the class map <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"j\">\\(j\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LargeEmbedding}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{LargeEmbedding}_S\\)</span> is the large-embedding metapredicate defined here</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}large\\text{-}embedding}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LargeEmbedding}_S(j,\\kappa,M)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Class}_S(M)\n\\land\\forall x\\in M\\;\\forall y\\in x\\;(y\\in M)\n\\land\\mathrm{ClassFunction}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j,V,M)\n\\land\\mathrm{ElementaryEmbedding}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j,(V,\\in),(M,\\in))\n\\land\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\kappa)\n\\land\\operatorname{crit}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j)=\\kappa\n\\land\\kappa&lt;j(\\kappa).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}large\\text{-}embedding}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LargeEmbedding}_S(j,\\kappa,M)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Class}_S(M)\n\\land\\forall x\\in M\\;\\forall y\\in x\\;(y\\in M)\n\\land\\mathrm{ClassFunction}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j,V,M)\n\\land\\mathrm{ElementaryEmbedding}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j,(V,\\in),(M,\\in))\n\\land\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\kappa)\n\\land\\operatorname{crit}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j)=\\kappa\n\\land\\kappa&lt;j(\\kappa).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ElementaryEmbedding}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j,(V,\\in),(M,\\in))\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{ElementaryClassEmbedding}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j,V,M).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{ElementaryEmbedding}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j,(V,\\in),(M,\\in))\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{ElementaryClassEmbedding}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j,V,M).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Large-cardinal embeddings are elementary class embeddings with a critical point. The set-coded <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ElementaryEmbedding}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ElementaryEmbedding}_S\\)</span> predicate is intentionally not applied to the proper class <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch03/58-df-large-cardinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"6a8560d21b03f127","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-df-large-cardinal.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch11/58-df-class.md","status":"resolved","id":"ca2a9c9166fa8cce","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_